Revision history for Perl extension Text::JSCalendar

0.10  unreleased
	- NormaliseEvent (and so CompareEvents) keeps what it does not know
	  instead of deleting it.  It used to delete every key missing from
	  its table, so every recurrenceOverrides patch normalised to {}
	  ({"excluded":true} compared equal to an RDATE), every alert trigger
	  to {} (any two alert offsets compared equal), and every @type was
	  stripped (an Event compared equal to a Task).  Now:
	  * unknown keys are kept, at every level
	  * override patches keep their contents; a patch value at a known
	    object path (participants/p1, alerts/a1/trigger, locations, ...)
	    is normalised as that object, and a patched value is never
	    dropped for being the default, since in a patch it overrides
	    the master
	  * an OffsetTrigger drops relativeTo "start" and an implied @type;
	    an AbsoluteTrigger or unknown trigger is kept whole
	  * @type is dropped only where the position implies it (Location,
	    Participant, Alert, NDay, ...); the Event or Task keeps it
	  * defaults follow jscalendarbis-22: status "confirmed", duration
	    "PT0S", descriptionContentType "text/plain", interval 1, and
	    scheduleAgent "server" (RFC 8984); participant kind has no
	    default, so "individual" no longer equals an unset kind
	  * a JSON false is now dropped where false is the default
	    (showWithoutTime, expectReply); it used to be kept because
	    JSON booleans are references
	  * a null map or array is dropped as before, but a malformed
	    value (a map that is not an object) is kept rather than dropped
	- t/icalfiles.t marks two round trips TODO that the old
	  NormaliseEvent hid (override patches lost on the way back)
	- add t/normalise.t
	- add t/roundtrip.t: JSCalendar -> iCalendar -> JSCalendar is the
	  identity for hand-written Events and Tasks using every converted
	  property (testdata/roundtrip/*.json), and iCalendar -> JSCalendar
	  -> iCalendar -> JSCalendar is stable for every .ics under testdata,
	  including the jscalendar-icalendar-29 examples
	  (tools/extract-icalendar-examples.pl).  Known conversion bugs are
	  TODO tests, each with its cause
	- MANIFEST lists the tests and test data added since 0.08
	- one bad component no longer costs the whole calendar.  The reader
	  converts each VEVENT/VTODO on its own, and each VALARM and RRULE
	  in it: a component that cannot be converted is dropped (an RRULE
	  with FREQ=FORTNIGHTLY used to confess, a VALARM without ACTION to
	  die on lc undef, each taking every event with it).  The writer
	  likewise writes each object, and each alert, on its own.  What was
	  dropped is reported by the new errors() method (uid, component,
	  id, message), reset by each vcalendarToEvents, eventsToVCalendar
	  or _argsToVCalendar call; their return values are unchanged
	- add t/isolation.t

0.09  2026-11-07
	- follows jscalendarbis-22, jscalendar-icalendar-29 and
	  icalendar-jscalendar-extensions-09
	- participant keys travel in the JSID parameter of ATTENDEE and
	  ORGANIZER, so an override patching participants/<key>/... still
	  finds its participant after a round trip
	- write each DELEGATED-TO/-FROM address as its own quoted value
	- links follow their rel: enclosure (the default when rel is unset)
	  is ATTACH, icon is IMAGE, the first describedby is URL, anything
	  else is LINK with LINKREL; title is FILENAME on ATTACH and IMAGE and
	  LABEL on URL and LINK.  Every non-enclosure link used to become URL,
	  so two of them made two URL properties.  URL reads as describedby,
	  LINK is read, IMAGE DISPLAY and SIZE are read, and every link is
	  keyed by its JSID
	- a floating time leaves timeZone unset instead of null
	- an unknown CLASS is private (it was public)
	- showWithoutTime no longer turns a timed event into a DATE one: DATE
	  only with no timeZone and no time of day; otherwise the time and
	  zone stay and SHOW-WITHOUT-TIME;VALUE=BOOLEAN:TRUE is written
	- a Task alert relative to end without a due is made relative to start
	- SENT-BY converts to the participant's sentBy, and the ORGANIZER's
	  also to the Event or Task sentBy, both ways
	- COLOR: an unreadable value is dropped instead of dying (which lost
	  the whole calendar); only valid COLOR values are written
	- RDATE;VALUE=PERIOD keeps the period's length as the override's
	  duration
	- add t/links.t, t/jscalendar-29.t, t/participant-jsid.t

0.08  2026-10-22
	- security: recurrenceOverrides patches could rewrite top-level-only
	  properties when writing iCalendar, e.g. "uid" (exception emitted
	  under a foreign UID, splitting the series), "@type" (a VTODO in a
	  VEVENT's recurrence set) or "recurrenceRule"; such patches are
	  now ignored, as they already were when reading iCalendar
	- security: strip control characters from iCalendar output; a CR or
	  LF in any field written as a property parameter (participant name,
	  descriptionContentType, locale, link title, ...), or a lone CR in a
	  value, could split the content line and forge extra properties
	- top-level-only properties updated to jscalendarbis-21: add @type,
	  privacy, sentBy, recurrenceId, recurrenceIdTimeZone and
	  participants/*/calendarAddress; relatedTo may now be overridden
	- a synthetic master built from orphan exceptions now has @type
	  and version, so neither turns up as a patch in every override
	- write an ATTENDEE for every participant with a calendarAddress, as
	  jscalendarbis has no "attendee" role; a participant that the
	  ORGANIZER fully represents is still left out
	- a change inside an object in a recurrence exception is now a nested
	  patch (e.g. one attendee's participationStatus) rather than a copy
	  of the whole object

0.07  2026-10-09
	- write each participant's ATTENDEE from its jscalendarbis
	  calendarAddress URI, falling back to the JSCalendar 1.0 "email";
	  previously only "email" was read, so a jscalendarbis participant
	  produced "MAILTO:" with an undefined address
	- skip a participant with neither address rather than writing an
	  empty ATTENDEE

0.06  2026-08-31
	- clarify licensing: same terms as Perl itself (Artistic License 1.0
	  or GPL version 1 or later)
	- include a LICENSE file in the distribution
	- POD and README previously claimed Artistic License 2.0, which
	  contradicted the Perl_5 metadata; the POD/README were wrong

0.05  2026-05-11
	- jscalendarbis-15 (draft-ietf-calext-jscalendarbis-15) compliance:
	- recurrenceRule is now a singular object (not the RFC 8984 plural array)
	- Add organizerCalendarAddress top-level property; remove replyTo
	- Add endTimeZone top-level Event property
	- Remove useDefaultAlerts (and X-APPLE-DEFAULT-ALARM handling)
	- Add version: "2.0" to all parsed events
	- Rename byDate -> byMonthDay in RecurrenceRule
	- Fix firstDayOfWeek default "monday" -> "mo"
	- Restructure alerts: flat {action,relativeTo,offset} ->
	  {action, trigger: OffsetTrigger/AbsoluteTrigger}; restore action field
	- Fix TRIGGER RELATED=END: written as parameter on TRIGGER not standalone property
	- Rename links[*].type -> contentType; remove links[*].cid
	- Link.display type changed to String[Boolean]
	- Location: remove description, relativeTo, timeZone sub-properties
	- VirtualLocation: remove description sub-property
	- Participant: sendTo -> calendarAddress (single URI string)
	- Participant: kind default changed to "individual"
	- Participant: remove language; add description, descriptionContentType,
	  progressUpdated, links
	- Participants roles: String[Boolean] map (was String[] array)
	- privacy: CLASS:CONFIDENTIAL now maps to "secret"
	- task.progress: use "in-process" (correct JSCalendar value)
	- Add excludedRecurrenceRules support (EXRULE) and remove again: jscalendarbis
	  drops excludedRecurrenceRules entirely; exclusions via recurrenceOverrides only
	- Add @type to RecurrenceRule, NDay, Relation, VirtualLocation, Location sub-objects
	- relatedTo: type changed from keywords to object (with Relation sub-schema)
	- Remove isAllDay (replaced by showWithoutTime)
	- Remove endTimeZone that was removed in 0.04 draft work, then re-added
	- Remove lastModified (use updated instead)
	- Remove organizerCalendarAddress that was removed in 0.04 draft work, then re-added

0.04  2026-05-11
	- RFC 8984 compliance fixes (superseded by 0.05 jscalendarbis work):
	- Remove isAllDay (replaced by showWithoutTime)
	- Rename recurrenceRule to recurrenceRules (array per RFC 8984)
	- Remove endTimeZone (not in RFC 8984)
	- Remove lastModified (use updated instead)
	- Remove organizerCalendarAddress (use participants with role=owner)
	- Replace attendance field with roles (optional/informational) in participants

0.03  2026-04-05
	- Update for latest JSCalendar drafts (jscalendarbis,
	  jscalendar-icalendar, icalendar-jscalendar-extensions)
	- Add virtualLocations (CONFERENCE property)
	- Add endTimeZone (replaces locations[end] hack)
	- Add GEO -> locations[].coordinates
	- Fix privacy/CLASS property bug
	- Add priority, color, lastModified generation
	- Add STYLED-DESCRIPTION -> descriptionContentType
	- Add showWithoutTime alongside isAllDay
	- freeBusyStatus is now a string (was boolean showAsFree)
	- Add organizerCalendarAddress
	- Add IMAGE -> links, binary ATTACH -> data: URI
	- Add VTODO/Task support
	- Add participant scheduleAgent, delegatedFrom/To, ROLE=OWNER
	- @type updated to Event/Task per JSCalendar bis
	- Add Cyrus CalDAV/JMAP integration tests

0.02  2019-03-24
	- add tests
	- fix up participation status
	- heaps of bugfixes (but plenty more known incompleteness)

0.01  2019-02-09
	- original release
